cl.historia.0.titulo=The crash
cl.historia.0.0=Your ship crashed on a desert planet, with no water and no one around. The hull held together and became your shelter: inside there is light, the cockpit and a chest with what is left of the cargo.
cl.historia.0.1=Four systems burned in the crash: §6hull§r, §6flight computer§r, §6fuel§r and §6engine§r. No one is coming for you. The only way out is to repair the ship and take off.
cl.historia.1.titulo=First days
cl.historia.1.0=Take the §bWater Condenser§r from the plane's chest and place it: it pulls water from the air. Plant the saplings and make your first tools.
cl.historia.1.1=There is no ore and no stone here: under the sand there is only sandstone. In the §6sieve§r, dirt drops pebbles (4 = 1 cobblestone); with the §6hammer§r, cobblestone turns into gravel, gravel into sand and sand into dust; sieved, they drop ores, seeds and more.
cl.historia.1.2=Follow this Journal: each quest teaches the next step and gives a reward.
cl.historia.2.titulo=Water, heat and thirst
cl.historia.2.0=The §bWater§r bar and your §6Body§r temperature sit at the bottom of the screen. Under the midday sun your body heats up: stay in the shade and drink. Thirst and heatstroke hurt.
cl.historia.2.1=Salt or dirty water is not safe to drink: boil it in a furnace, a campfire or a cauldron over fire. The §bCamel Pack§r carries water with you.
cl.historia.3.titulo=Day and night
cl.historia.3.0=By day the desert is calm: monsters bury themselves in the sand and nothing spawns on the surface. At night they come out. Stay near the plane or build a lit shelter.
cl.historia.3.1=Every 10 nights a §chorde§r comes, with a warning at dusk. Sandstorms bring the Sand Golem. When you are safe, the §6Sleeping Bag§r skips the night.
cl.historia.3.2=No animals live here: they arrive in the §6cargo capsules§r that fall from the sky.
cl.historia.4.titulo=Technology
cl.historia.4.0=With power (generator, solar panel, batteries and cables) come the machines: they multiply ores, make parts and automate the work. Each mod has a chapter in this Journal.
cl.historia.4.1=The §bCatalog§r shows how to make any item and where it is used. Crafting recipes also show in the inventory recipe book.
cl.historia.4.2=Look for abandoned cities (they have a radio signal), wrecks and dungeons: they hold parts that cannot be crafted.
cl.historia.5.titulo=Going home
cl.historia.5.0=Gather the parts for the four systems and repair each one at the §6Ship Panel§r, in the plane's cockpit. With everything fixed, the panel shows the §aTAKE OFF§r button.
cl.historia.5.1=After take-off the world goes on, with new challenges in the Journal. Good luck, pilot.
cl.historia.botao=§6Read first: what happened
