cl.tc.tracodesc.airborne=Tool no longer is penalized when mining in the air and gains a projectile velocity bonus
cl.tc.tracodesc.ambush=Deals more damage when you or the target is at full health.
cl.tc.tracodesc.antitoxin=Tool does more damage and draws faster when poisoned
cl.tc.tracodesc.conducting=Tool deals multiplied damage when you are on fire
cl.tc.tracodesc.cultivated=Tool practically grows more material when repairing
cl.tc.tracodesc.dense=Tool lasts longer, but is harder to repair
cl.tc.tracodesc.ductile=Tool is longer lasting, damages more and is tougher
cl.tc.tracodesc.dwarven=Tool mines faster and has more projectile velocity the deeper you mine, but loses effectiveness if you go too high
cl.tc.tracodesc.enderference=Prevents target from teleporting for a short time
cl.tc.tracodesc.enderporting=Tool teleports the holder to mined blocks or killed entities
cl.tc.tracodesc.enhanced=Rose gold goes great with a bonus upgrade slot!
cl.tc.tracodesc.entangled=Increases speed or knockback resistance at the cost of taking damage when unequipping
cl.tc.tracodesc.flamestance=Increases power and protection in hot biomes, but reduces it in cold biomes
cl.tc.tracodesc.harvest=Tool can be used on crops to harvest and replant them
cl.tc.tracodesc.jagged=Every point durability lost increases damage, but decreases mining speed
cl.tc.tracodesc.knockback=Hitting things in melee makes them go flying further!
cl.tc.tracodesc.lacerating=Causes the target to bleed, dealing additional damage
cl.tc.tracodesc.lightweight=Tool is incredibly light for its size, allowing you to attack, mine, and launch projectiles faster
cl.tc.tracodesc.looting=Gives you more nice things when killing mobs!
cl.tc.tracodesc.magnetic=Hitting things attracts nearby items?!
cl.tc.tracodesc.maintained=Tool mines faster when at higher durability
cl.tc.tracodesc.momentum=Mining blocks and firing arrows increases your speed, as long as you keep going
cl.tc.tracodesc.necrotic=Critical hits on enemies drains their life to heal you
cl.tc.tracodesc.offhand_attack=
cl.tc.tracodesc.overburn=Tool converts liquid fuel into overslime
cl.tc.tracodesc.overcast=Overslime can be made extra thick on this tool
cl.tc.tracodesc.overgrowth=Tool slowly grows overslime
cl.tc.tracodesc.overlord=Tool takes some of the durability as new overslime subjects
cl.tc.tracodesc.overslime=Tool consumes overslime instead of durability, until it runs out! Not friendly towards tools lacking slime
cl.tc.tracodesc.overslime_friend=Counts as a slimy material, preventing overslime from debuffing the tool
cl.tc.tracodesc.overwield=Consumes overslime to boost mining speed, attack speed, drawspeed, and projectile velocity
cl.tc.tracodesc.overworked=Increases amount of overslime restored from all sources
cl.tc.tracodesc.padded=Reduces the knockback of the tool, to stop your enemies from escaping
cl.tc.tracodesc.pathing=Tool can make paths
cl.tc.tracodesc.pierce=Attacks cancels out some of the target's armor!
cl.tc.tracodesc.preserved=Makes the tool more durable and easier to repair
cl.tc.tracodesc.scorching=Tool does bonus damage to targets that are on fire
cl.tc.tracodesc.searing=Tool mines meltable blocks such as metal ores faster
cl.tc.tracodesc.severing=Potentially blasts heads or other parts of targets of melee right off!
cl.tc.tracodesc.shears=Tool can be used to shear mobs and disarm tripwire
cl.tc.tracodesc.silky_shears=Tool can shear mobs if the silky modifier is added
cl.tc.tracodesc.smite=Undead fear the might of the melon!
cl.tc.tracodesc.solar_powered=Tool resists damage in sunlight
cl.tc.tracodesc.spiny=Boosts the projectile's damage, but damages you when used.
cl.tc.tracodesc.stonebound=The tool mines faster as it wears out, but does less damage
cl.tc.tracodesc.stoneshield=Mined stone has a chance to protect the tool from future damage
cl.tc.tracodesc.stringy=Tool can be repaired using string
cl.tc.tracodesc.stripping=Tool can strip bark from wood
cl.tc.tracodesc.tanned=Tool no longer takes double or more damage from certain actions
