## Dicas da tela de carregamento (gerado por tools/gerar-dicas.mjs)
beginnerTips.1=Your ship crashed, but the hull is a shelter: at night, stay inside the plane or somewhere lit.
beginnerTips.2=Open the Logbook: each quest teaches the next step and gives a reward.
beginnerTips.3=There is no stone or ore underground: everything comes from the sieve. Sieved dirt gives pebbles (4 = 1 cobblestone).
beginnerTips.4=Dirt: fill a Wooden Barrel with 8 leaves or saplings (or dead bushes, cacti, rotten flesh) and wait 1 minute.
beginnerTips.5=Iron: sieve sand. 1 in 5 gives Crushed Iron Ore, and 4 of them make 1 raw iron.
beginnerTips.6=Minecraft tools are awful here (slow and wear 8× faster). Build the Tinkers tools.
beginnerTips.7=Before the Water Condenser, drink the jars in the plane's chest, the water in the wrecks and boiled cactus water.
beginnerTips.8=There is almost no ore in sight: with a hammer, stone becomes gravel, gravel becomes sand and sand becomes dust.
beginnerTips.9=In the Sieve, gravel, sand and dust drop ores, seeds and more.
beginnerTips.10=Under the midday sun your body heats up: stay in the shade and drink water.
beginnerTips.11=Salt or dirty water is not safe to drink: boil it in a furnace, on a campfire or in a cauldron over fire.
beginnerTips.12=By day monsters bury themselves in the sand. At night they come back.
midgameTips.1=Your ship crashed, but the hull is a shelter: at night, stay inside the plane or somewhere lit.
midgameTips.2=Open the Logbook: each quest teaches the next step and gives a reward.
midgameTips.3=There is no stone or ore underground: everything comes from the sieve. Sieved dirt gives pebbles (4 = 1 cobblestone).
midgameTips.4=Dirt: fill a Wooden Barrel with 8 leaves or saplings (or dead bushes, cacti, rotten flesh) and wait 1 minute.
midgameTips.5=Iron: sieve sand. 1 in 5 gives Crushed Iron Ore, and 4 of them make 1 raw iron.
midgameTips.6=Minecraft tools are awful here (slow and wear 8× faster). Build the Tinkers tools.
midgameTips.7=Before the Water Condenser, drink the jars in the plane's chest, the water in the wrecks and boiled cactus water.
midgameTips.8=There is almost no ore in sight: with a hammer, stone becomes gravel, gravel becomes sand and sand becomes dust.
midgameTips.9=In the Sieve, gravel, sand and dust drop ores, seeds and more.
midgameTips.10=Under the midday sun your body heats up: stay in the shade and drink water.
midgameTips.11=Salt or dirty water is not safe to drink: boil it in a furnace, on a campfire or in a cauldron over fire.
midgameTips.12=By day monsters bury themselves in the sand. At night they come back.
midgameTips.13=No animals live here: they arrive in the cargo capsules that fall from the sky.
midgameTips.14=The Catalog shows how to make any item and where it is used.
midgameTips.15=Every crafting recipe shows up in the inventory recipe book.
midgameTips.16=Lost? The Plane Compass shows which way and how far the Ship Console is.
midgameTips.17=Every 10 nights a horde comes, with a warning at dusk. Get your defenses ready.
midgameTips.18=Sandstorms bring the Sand Golem.
midgameTips.19=When you are safe, the Sleeping Bag skips the night.
midgameTips.20=The Camel Pack carries water with you on long trips.
midgameTips.21=Eating the same thing gets old: the game remembers your last 12 meals. Vary your diet.
midgameTips.22=Date palm saplings come from sifting sand, and they grow bunches of dates.
midgameTips.23=The Drying Rack dries raw meat into Beef Jerky.
midgameTips.24=Abandoned cities have a radio signal: they hold parts that cannot be crafted.
midgameTips.25=Saw a meteor fall? The coordinates show in chat. Meteorite rock drops ores and sometimes diamond.
midgameTips.26=Power first: a generator, solar panels, batteries and cables open the way to machines.
midgameTips.27=Machines multiply ores: one ore can yield more than one ingot.
midgameTips.28=Tinkers' tools can be repaired and gain modifiers at the Tool Station.
midgameTips.29=Oil lies deep below the sand. The Pump extracts it and the Refinery makes fuel.
midgameTips.30=Hold the Hang Glider while falling to glide forward. Sneak to close it.
midgameTips.31=Two Elevators, one above the other: jump to go up, sneak to go down.
midgameTips.32=When you die, your items go into a Grave on the spot, with the coordinates in chat.
midgameTips.33=Storage Barrels hold a lot of a single item.
midgameTips.34=In an AE network all items are stored together and the terminal finds any of them.
midgameTips.35=There is no air on the Moon: wear the Oxygen Mask and Oxygen Gear and carry full tanks. A light tank lasts almost 7 minutes.
midgameTips.36=The rocket lands on the Moon, but only lifts off from a 3×3 pad: bring 9 pads, a fuel loader and power.
midgameTips.37=The Mekanism paxel is a pickaxe, an axe and a shovel in one tool.
midgameTips.38=The Mekanism Wind Generator makes more power the higher it is.
midgameTips.39=Cooking Pot on top of fire or a Stove: tap with the ingredients and, when it is done, serve with a bowl.
midgameTips.40=Tap a ripe crop to harvest it: it replants itself (Quark).
midgameTips.41=Item Conduit: tap it so the core turns orange and it pulls items from the touching chest to the other chests on the network.
midgameTips.42=A Mekanism balloon used in the air makes you fall slowly for a minute.
midgameTips.43=Put a Waystone at each base: tapping one takes you to any other you have activated.
midgameTips.44=The Mining Turtle digs on its own: refuel it with coal and pick tunnel or excavate. Leave a chest behind it.
midgameTips.45=The Backpack becomes a chest on the ground: use the Open button and hit it to pick it up.
midgameTips.46=In Create, tap a cogwheel to see RPM and stress: if machines need more SU than the sources give, everything stops.
midgameTips.47=A Water Wheel touching water spins forever: connect it with shafts to a Millstone to make flour.
midgameTips.48=Two Ender IO Travel Anchors within 96 blocks: tap one to travel to the other.
midgameTips.49=The Nether portal won't light here: a hammer turns netherrack into Nether Gravel, and sifting it gives quartz and even netherite.
midgameTips.50=Four systems burned in the crash: hull, flight computer, fuel and engine.
midgameTips.51=The Ship Console in the plane's cockpit repairs each system once you have the parts.
midgameTips.52=With all four systems repaired, the Jump Coil is still missing: the Jump Core is in the lunar research base.
midgameTips.53=On the Moon, the Plane Compass points to the research base signal.
midgameTips.54=No one is coming for you. The only way out is to repair the ship and take off.
midgameTips.55=Each mod has a chapter in the Logbook. Follow it to the end to go home.
midgameTips.56=Your ship crashed, but the hull is a shelter: at night, stay inside the plane or somewhere lit.
